  "schema": "agv.coverage.tail.v2",
  "question": "why every pass reported an unverified strip at its far end, and one pass at its near end",
  "tail_cause": "capture closed 0.10 m past the region end while the sensor discards a closing image below min_tail_rows (1000 lines x 0.3662109375 mm = 0.3662 m), so the discarded stretch always came out of the region; the audit then shrank each span by coverage_error_m",
  "tail_fix": "planner derives scan_overrun_distance_m = min_tail_rows*line_spacing + 2*coverage_error = 0.5662 m and floors the run-out with it; worst-case discard is 999 lines = 0.3658 m, so the last archived row lands at least 0.2004 m past the region end against the 0.112 m the audit needs -- a bound, not an observed remainder, so it does not depend on track length",
  "head_cause": "capture was acknowledged before the pass re-steered, so the wheel alignment crept under an open shutter; the resulting ALIGN_WHEEL_MOTION quality window overlapped the first image by 11-18 ms and the conservative whole-block exclusion dropped 1.5 m",
  "head_fix": "capture opens once the controller reaches DRIVE, measured 4-20 ms of handshake against 0.6 m of remaining lead-in; the implicit \"do not move before the sensor acknowledges\" is replaced by an explicit CAPTURE_NOT_ACTIVE_AT_REGION fault at the region edge",
  "mission": "7 passes, GUI + RViz + OptiX, 1.0 m/s",
